From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] toys.h: don't include <paths.h> on NuttX

NuttX has no <paths.h>, so this include ends the build before a single
applet is compiled.

lib/portability.h already knows that and defines _PATH_DEFPATH -- the one
thing the compiled set uses from that header -- for NuttX itself. The
include was simply left behind, which goes unnoticed on the sim board this
port documents as its example, because a Linux host supplies a real
<paths.h> from /usr/include.

Guarded rather than deleted: every other platform still wants it, and on
those it is where _PATH_DEFPATH comes from.
---
 toys.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/toys.h b/toys.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/toys.h
+++ b/toys.h
@@ -17,7 +17,9 @@
 #include <inttypes.h>
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <math.h>
+#ifndef __NuttX__
 #include <paths.h>
+#endif
 #include <pwd.h>
 #include <regex.h>
 #include <sched.h>
